{
  "id": "COMPOUND:33837 - PROTEIN:1642",
  "verbalization": "Calanphenanthrene A is implicated in the activation of Proto-oncogene tyrosine-protein kinase Src through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Calanphenanthrene A directly targets Isoleucine--tRNA ligase, which in turn is a target of Jasplakinolide Z1 and Paeonilide. These compounds are known to interact with tyrosine-protein kinase Src, indicating a potential pathway where Calanphenanthrene A may exert its effects by modulating the activity of these enzymes. The shared target of Src in all three pathways underscores a possible mechanism by which Calanphenanthrene A influences cellular processes, potentially through the regulation of protein kinases involved in signal transduction. The integration of these findings highlights a convergent relationship between Calanphenanthrene A and Src, suggesting a role in oncogenic processes through the modulation of key regulatory enzymes.",
